# Publish & live deploy (Loot & Lasers)

## “Commit, push, and deploy” (and equivalents)

When the user says **commit and push**, **commit, push, and deploy**, or equivalent, do **all** of the following:

1. **Commit locally** per `git-commit-convention.mdc` (milestone commits; no secrets).
2. **Push to GitHub** — `git -c credential.helper=manager push origin HEAD` (normally `main`) when the agent shell has no default credential helper; otherwise `git push origin HEAD`.
3. **Deploy Hetzner Node API** — run `scripts/deploy-hetzner-node-api.ps1` from the local checkout (default SSH identity: `%USERPROFILE%\Desktop\LootLasers\SSH\Farts`).
4. **Deploy / reload Nakama** on staging — keep modules current; recreate/reload Nakama as needed (**no game-data wipe**). See `docs/STAGING_NAKAMA.md` / host compose under `/opt/lootandlasers`.
5. **Never** build a Windows installer / Godot export unless the user **explicitly** asks for one.

## Targets

| Target | On “commit, push, and deploy” | Who |
|--------|-------------------------------|-----|
| **Local repo / GitHub Desktop** | Yes — `git commit` | Agent |
| **GitHub.com remote (`origin`)** | Yes — `git push` to the live branch (usually `main`) | Agent |
| **Hetzner Node API** | Yes — deploy | Agent |
| **Nakama** | Yes — reload/deploy | Agent |
| **Godot installer** | Only if asked | Agent when requested |

## Do not

- Skip the GitHub push when the user asked to push/deploy live.
- Skip Hetzner/Nakama when they said commit and push / commit, push, and deploy.
- Force-push to `main`/`master` unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Wipe Nakama / Cockroach / player data as part of a normal deploy.
- Build an installer unless explicitly requested.
